From 5ca6ca6bdf6bc25ac1232293232ea3e6624fb7ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brayanspagnol <121728908+brayanspagnol@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:39:57 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Wasm: keep context symbols in locals (context promotion),
 name section

CCodeGen_Wasm can now keep relative (context) symbols that are only accessed as
one whole symbol in wasm locals for the whole function: they are loaded at entry,
stored back at exit and around calls. Context arrays reached through references
must be registered (RegisterContextArray); symbols inside them stay in memory and
a function that references an unregistered part of the context is not promoted.
Off by default (SetContextPromotion).

Also: optional function name (name custom section) for profiling, and fix the
local declaration size when a local group has more than 127 entries.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
