From e44a2cf7e8da3432438667f073bbd8cd5d7770b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brayanspagnol <121728908+brayanspagnol@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:24:13 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Wasm: promote 128-bit context symbols together with their
 lanes

Context promotion now groups accesses into containers: a 128-bit symbol keeps
32/64-bit accesses inside it as lanes (extract_lane/replace_lane on the v128
local), and an f32 access to the same place as an i32 symbol is a bitcast of
the i32 local. Before, any partial overlap left both symbols in memory.

